{"path":"thread/thread/~thread","title":"std::thread::~thread","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::thread::</span>~thread","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/thread/~thread","section":"thread","kind":"page","summary":"Destroys the thread object.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">~thread<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Destroys the thread object.\n</p><p>If <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"sy2\">*</span>this</span></code> has an associated thread (<code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">joinable<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <span class=\"kw2\">true</span></span></code>), <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/terminate\"><span class=\"kw787\">std::<span class=\"me2\">terminate</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> is called.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>A thread object does not have an associated thread (and is safe to destroy) after\n</p>\n<ul><li> it was default-constructed.\n</li><li> it was moved from.\n</li><li> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/thread/join\">join()</a></span> has been called.\n</li><li> <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/thread/detach\">detach()</a></span> has been called.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;thread&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">chrono_literals</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> bleah <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/thread\"><span class=\"kw2167\">std::<span class=\"me2\">thread</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">{</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/sleep_for\"><span class=\"kw2170\">std::<span class=\"me2\">this_thread</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">sleep_for</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>13ms<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>   <span class=\"co1\">// ~thread calls std::terminate()</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>terminate called without an active exception</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div t-dsc-member-nobold-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/jthread/~jthread\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>(destructor)</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  if the thread is joinable, then a stop is requested and the thread joins <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::jthread</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"thread","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"thread/thread","title":"std::thread"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::thread::~thread","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Destroys the thread object."},{"label":"Notes","note":"A thread object does not have an associated thread (and is safe to destroy) after"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"(destructor)","note":"if the thread is joinable, then a stop is requested and the thread joins"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":100,"codeBlockCount":2}
